# Coop Use — React Native Project Rules

You are a senior React Native engineer working on this codebase. Follow the
conventions below exactly. They are derived from the real code, not generic
best practices. When in doubt, mirror existing files.

## 1. Tech Stack (Core Libraries)

- **Runtime**: React Native 0.81.5, React 19.1, TypeScript 5.8 (strict).
- **Navigation**: `@react-navigation/native` v7 + `@react-navigation/stack` +
  `@react-navigation/bottom-tabs` (native-stack is NOT used). Two stacks
  (`Auth` / `App`) defined in `navigation/Stacks.tsx`; tabs in
  `AppTabNavigator.tsx`. Imperative navigation goes through the global
  `AppNavigator` service (`navigation/AppNavigator.tsx`) — navigate, reset,
  goBack, getParams, getPreviousRoute, plus dialog helpers
  (`showLoading`/`hideLoading`, snackbar).
- **State management**: Redux Toolkit + `react-redux`, `redux-saga` for async
  side effects. `thunk` is DISABLED in the store; do async work in sagas.
- **Persistence**: `redux-persist` backed by `react-native-mmkv`
  (`services/common/storage.ts`). MMKV is the ONLY local storage.
- **HTTP**: `axios` wrapped by `httpRequest` (`services/common/httpRequest.ts`).
- **Validation**: `zod` v4 — response schemas live next to request functions
  in `services/request/`.
- **Realtime**: STOMP over WebSocket (`@stomp/stompjs` + `sockjs-client`) via
  `WebSocketService` in `services/common/webSocket.ts`.
- **Push notifications**: `react-native-onesignal` (push id registered via
  `EndPoints.ACCOUNT.updatePushId`).
- **Social login**: Google (`@react-native-google-signin`), Kakao
  (`@react-native-seoul/kakao-login`), Naver (`@react-native-seoul/naver-login`).
- **i18n**: `i18next` + `react-i18next`. Locales: `en-EN.json` + `ko-KR.json`
  (English + Korean — there is NO French). Language persisted in MMKV.
- **UI/UX libs**: `react-native-reanimated` v4 (+ carousel, skeleton), core
  `Animated` for collapsing headers, `@d11/react-native-fast-image` surfaced
  through the shared `<Image />` component, `react-native-svg` for icons,
  `react-native-linear-gradient`, `react-native-render-html`,
  `react-native-qrcode-svg` / `react-native-barcode-creator`.
- **Scaling**: `ScaleSize` from `@kits/core` — REQUIRED for every numeric UI
  value (see §4).
- **Dates**: `dayjs`. **Utils**: `lodash`. **Debugging**: Reactotron.
- **Env/config**: `react-native-config`, ENVFILE-based (`env/.dev`), surfaced
  ONLY through the `Environment` object in `constants/environment.ts`
  (`BASE_URL`, `ONE_SIGNAL_ID`, `DOMAIN_CDN`, social keys...). Never read
  `Config` directly elsewhere; never hardcode hosts.
- There is NO Firebase and NO analytics SDK.

## 2. Directory Structure

- `src/App.tsx` — root: `GestureHandlerRootView`, redux `Provider`,
  `PersistGate`, navigator.
- `src/navigation/` — `Application.tsx` (container), `Stacks.tsx` (Auth/App
  stack definitions as `ScreenDef[]` arrays), `AppTabNavigator.tsx` (bottom
  tabs), `AppNavigator.tsx` (imperative navigation + dialog service),
  `paths.ts` (`Paths` + `AppStacks` enums), `types.ts`
  (`RootStackParamList`, `RootScreenProps`), `deepLinkGate.ts`,
  `FloatingCartButton.tsx`.
- `src/screens/` — one folder per screen: `<Name>/index.tsx` plus co-located
  section components (`Products/HeroHeader.tsx`, `Products/ProductRow.tsx`...)
  or a `components/` subfolder for bigger screens (`Authorisation/components/
  LoginForm/`...). `screens/index.ts` re-exports every screen (used by
  `Stacks.tsx`). `screens/Dialog/components` is aliased as `@dialogs`.
- `src/components/` — shared presentational components, one folder each with
  `index.tsx` (`AppButton`, `TextField`, `Image`, `EmptyView`...).
- `src/hooks/` — one `use<Screen>.ts` hook per screen holding ALL screen logic
  (state, pagination, dispatch, navigation). `hooks/index.ts` re-exports.
  `language/` groups i18n hooks.
- `src/services/`:
  - `common/` — `store.ts`, `instance.ts` (axios + auth interceptors),
    `httpRequest.ts`, `storage.ts` (MMKV), `rootSaga.ts`, `storeHooks.ts`
    (typed `useAppDispatch`/`useAppSelector`), `webSocket.ts` (STOMP).
  - `request/<domain>.ts` — plain async API functions per domain
    (`auth.ts`, `products.ts`, `payment.ts`, `wallet.ts`...). This is the ONLY
    place that calls `httpRequest`.
  - `slices/<feature>/` — `<feature>Slice.ts` + `<feature>Saga.ts`
    (account, app, auth, notifications, payment, products, stores, survey).
  - `selectors/<feature>.ts` — selector functions grouped in a
    `<Feature>Selector` object (e.g. `AuthSelector.getAccessToken`).
  - `native/AppNativeModules.ts` — native module bridge.
- `src/constants/` — `api.ts` (`EndPoints` — ALL endpoint paths live here),
  `config.ts` (business constants: auth steps, membership types,
  `HISLOP_BUTTON`...), `environment.ts` (`Environment`), `theme.ts`
  (`Colors`, `Fonts`), re-exported via `index.ts` (`@constants`).
- `src/types/` (`@type`) — per-domain types: `common.ts`
  (`SingleApiResponse<T>`, `ListApiResponse<T>`), `auth.ts`, `products.ts`...
- `src/utils/` (`@utils`) — `common.ts` (`getErrorMessageApi`, `CommonUtils`),
  `product.ts` (`formatCurrency`), `Globals.ts`.
- `src/assets/` — `icons/` (svg + registry), `images/` (registry + generated
  `names.ts`; regenerate with `yarn icons` / `yarn images`).
- `src/translations/` — i18n setup, `en-EN.json`, `ko-KR.json`, `i18next.d.ts`.
- `src/tests/` — `TestAppWrapper.tsx` + `__mocks__/`.
- `kits/core/` (`@kits/core`) — device-independent kit: `ScaleSize`
  (responsive size, from `utils/reponsiveSize.ts`) and `utils/`
  (`DeviceUtils`, `NumberUtils`, `ValidateUtils`, `CommonUtils`,
  `FileManager`).
- Ignore `android/`, `ios/`, `node_modules/`, `scripts/`, `patches/`.

## 3. Path Aliases

Always import via aliases, never deep relative paths across folders:
`@assets/*`, `@components` / `@components/*`, `@dialogs` / `@dialogs/*`,
`@hooks` / `@hooks/*`, `@navigation/*`, `@screens` / `@screens/*`,
`@services/*`, `@translations` / `@translations/*`, `@tests/*`,
`@type` / `@type/*`, `@utils` / `@utils/*`, `@constants` / `@constants/*`,
`@kits/*`. Relative imports only for siblings in the same folder
(e.g. `Products/index.tsx` importing `./HeroHeader`).

## 4. Coding Conventions

### UI sizing — ScaleSize (MANDATORY)
- EVERY numeric style value (fontSize, padding, margin, width, height,
  borderRadius, icon size...) must be wrapped in `ScaleSize(n)` from
  `@kits/core`: `fontSize: ScaleSize(16)`. Never hardcode raw numbers in
  styles. Signature: `ScaleSize(size, iPadSize?, pixelSize?)` — optional
  second arg overrides on iPad/tablet.

### Components & screens
- Prefer `function Component() {}` declarations, then `export default`.
- Wrap presentational reusable components in `React.memo` (see `AppButton`).
- When a screen's render tree grows large, SPLIT it: extract sections
  (header, row, empty view, form...) into co-located files in the screen
  folder (`HeroHeader.tsx`, `ProductRow.tsx`, `ListEmpty.tsx`) or a
  `components/` subfolder; promote to `src/components/` only if reused.
- Screen logic does NOT live in the screen component: put it in a
  `src/hooks/use<Screen>.ts` hook and destructure what the JSX needs
  (see `Products/index.tsx` + `useProducts.ts`).
- Styles via `StyleSheet.create`, declared AFTER the component, named `styles`.
- Colors come from `Colors` in `@constants` (theme.ts); file-local one-off
  colors are declared as top-level constants.
- Use `SafeAreaView`/`useSafeAreaInsets` from `react-native-safe-area-context`
  (not core RN).
- Buttons: use the shared `AppButton` (TouchableOpacity + `activeOpacity` +
  `HISLOP_BUTTON` hitSlop). Provide `testID` on interactive elements.
- Props type is named `Properties` or `<Name>Props`; mark fields `readonly`.
- Constants: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` at module top (`HERO_HEIGHT`,
  `REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS`). Magic numbers are lint errors (only -1..6 inline).

### TypeScript & lint (STRICT — eslint blocks merges)
- `type` only — `interface` is forbidden (`consistent-type-definitions`).
- Use `import type { ... }` for type-only imports.
- ESLint `perfectionist` enforces ALPHABETICAL ordering of object keys, object
  types, JSX props, and union members.
- Strict type-checked + unicorn rules. Avoid `any`; model absence with
  `T | undefined` (the codebase uses `undefined`, not `null`).
- `console.log` is banned; only `console.warn` / `console.error`.
- Run `yarn lint` (rules + prettier + tsc) before considering work done.

## 5. Standard Flows

### API call flow (follow `products` end-to-end as the reference)
1. Add the endpoint path to `EndPoints` in `constants/api.ts` (list endpoints
   take a pre-built query string: `list: (request: string) => \`product?${request}\``).
2. Define request/response types in `src/types/<domain>.ts`. Responses are
   wrapped: `SingleApiResponse<T>` / `ListApiResponse<T>` from `@type/common`.
   Add a `zod` schema in the request file when validation is needed.
3. Write the request function in `services/request/<domain>.ts`:
   ```ts
   export const getProducts = async (request: GetProductsPayload) => {
     const params = CommonUtils.objectToQueryParams(
       CommonUtils.removeEmptyFieldObject(request, true));
     const response = await httpRequest.get<SingleApiResponse<ListApiResponse<Product[]>>>(
       EndPoints.PRODUCTS.list(params), { loading: false });
     return response.data;
   };
   ```
   `httpRequest` options: `loading` (default `true` — auto show/hide the
   global loading dialog via `AppNavigator`; pass `false` for silent calls),
   `retry`/`retryDelay` (retries ONLY network errors, never 4xx/5xx). It also
   attaches `x-device-*`/`x-app-*` headers automatically.
4. Add a "trigger" action in `<feature>Slice.ts` using `prepare`; the payload
   carries the request fields plus optional `onSuccess`/`onFailure` callbacks
   (the store's serializableCheck ignores `payload.onSuccess`/`payload.onFailure`).
   Reducers are often no-ops — server data usually stays in the calling hook's
   local state, not in redux.
5. Handle it in `<feature>Saga.ts` with `takeLatest`: `call` the request
   function, then `onSuccess?.(response)`; on error
   `onFailure?.(getErrorMessageApi(error))`.
6. Drive it from the screen's `use<Screen>.ts` hook: `dispatch(getProductsRequest({...request, onSuccess, onFailure}))`,
   keep list data / pagination (`currentPage`, `isLast`, load-more refs) in
   the hook's `useState`/`useRef`.
7. Register new reducers in `combineReducers` (`services/common/store.ts`) and
   new sagas via `fork` in `rootSaga.ts`.
8. Auth is automatic: `instance.ts` injects `Authorization: Bearer` from
   `store.getState().auth.accessToken`, and on 401 performs a single-flight
   refresh (`auth/refresh`), retries once (`_retry` guard), and on refresh
   failure clears credentials and resets navigation to the Auth stack. Do NOT
   create new axios instances for normal calls — reuse `instance`
   (`addressInstance` exists solely for the external address-lookup API).

### State flow
- Persistent/global state (tokens, profile, app settings): real reducers in a
  slice, mutate via Immer, read through `services/selectors/<feature>.ts`
  (`AuthSelector.getAccessToken`) with `useAppSelector`; dispatch with
  `useAppDispatch` (from `services/common/storeHooks.ts`). Never import raw
  `useSelector`/`useDispatch`.
- Screen-fetched data (lists, detail): keep it in the screen hook's local
  state via the saga callback pattern above — don't put it in redux unless
  another screen needs it.

### Navigation flow
- Add the route to the `Paths` enum (`navigation/paths.ts`) and
  `RootStackParamList` (`navigation/types.ts`).
- Register the screen in the right `ScreenDef[]` array (`AUTH_SCREENS` /
  app screens) in `navigation/Stacks.tsx`, and export it from
  `screens/index.ts`. Tab screens go in `AppTabNavigator.tsx`.
- Type screen props as `RootScreenProps<Paths.X>`; read params with
  `AppNavigator.getParams(props)`.
- Navigate imperatively via `AppNavigator.navigate(Paths.X, params)` /
  `AppNavigator.reset(AppStacks.X, {...})` — works outside components too
  (sagas, interceptors).
- Global dialogs/loading/snackbar also go through `AppNavigator`
  (`showLoading`, `hideLoading`, snackbar helpers backed by the `Dialog`
  screen; reusable dialog pieces live under `@dialogs`).

### WebSocket flow
- Use the `WebSocketService` singleton (`services/common/webSocket.ts`) —
  STOMP client with reconnect + heartbeats; `connect(token)` after login,
  subscribe/unsubscribe topics through its API. Do not instantiate
  `Client` elsewhere.

## 6. Testing
- Jest + `@testing-library/react-native`.
- Render with `{ wrapper: TestAppWrapper }` (redux/i18n/safe-area provided).
  Query by `testID`, assert behavior via `fireEvent`.
- Co-locate tests as `*.test.tsx` next to the unit under test.

## 7. i18n
- All user-facing strings go through i18next (`useTranslation()` /
  `useI18n()` for switching); keys added to BOTH `en-EN.json` and
  `ko-KR.json`. Keys are grouped by feature (`choose_membership.join_student_title`).
  Language choice persists in MMKV under `appLanguage`.

## 8. Build & scripts
- `yarn ios` / `yarn android` (both use `ENVFILE=env/.dev`), `yarn pod`,
  `yarn xc` (open workspace), `yarn images` / `yarn icons` (regenerate asset
  registries), `yarn lint`, `yarn test`. Node >= 22, Yarn berry (3.6.4),
  `patch-package` runs on postinstall.
